_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:16:**Pivot Interiors** approaches System Setup as the platform-foundation layer for migration from D365 and HubSpot into NetSuite Orion. Its BRD covers subsidiary structure, integration architecture (HubSpot retained per Marketing §3.01 D-1; Comerica banking per Financial Management §3.08 D-6; SharePoint document management; UKG payroll per Financial Management §3.08), data migration scope, Orion-NetSuite-specific configurations including the merged role taxonomy, and configurations to support its operating cadence.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:18:Both companies share the same end-state goals: a single NetSuite Orion environment configured for the merged-company operating model, integrated with the platforms that remain (HubSpot for marketing, banking partners, payroll providers, document management), with role-based access supporting the merged-company organizational structure. Where they differ is largely in starting-state context (KBM coming from NetSuite Core; Pivot coming from D365 + HubSpot + multiple specialty platforms) and in the breadth of integration architecture.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:27:- Document migration to NetSuite File Cabinet and/or integrated document storage
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:41:- HubSpot integration architecture (per Marketing §3.01 D-1)
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:43:- SharePoint integration consideration (decided in D-3 below)
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:83:**Source:** KBM Google Drive integration (Marketing §3.01); Pivot SharePoint integration; cross-references CT-14
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:85:**KBM's approach.** KBM's existing document collaboration uses Google Drive, integrated with NetSuite via the Google Drive connector for opportunity, project, and RFP documents.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:87:**Pivot's approach.** Pivot's existing document management uses SharePoint, with a SharePoint integration listed as one of the considered SuiteApps.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:89:**Recommendation for the merged company.** Operate the merged company with NetSuite File Cabinet as the primary document repository for transactional documents (invoices, POs, contracts, signed proposals) and SharePoint as the merged-company collaboration-document platform. KBM's Google Drive content migrates to SharePoint on a defined transition timeline, with the Google Drive integration sunset once migration completes. The recommendation aligns with Pivot's existing operational footprint (SharePoint deployed and integrated into existing workflows), preserves the document-management discipline Pivot's teams already rely on, and removes the integration overhead of maintaining two collaboration platforms long-term. KBM users onboard into SharePoint as part of the Discovery → Activate transition.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:93:- (3a) Confirm: NetSuite File Cabinet as primary repository for transactional documents. *Recommended default: yes.*
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:94:- (3b) Confirm: SharePoint as merged-company collaboration-document platform with KBM Google Drive content migrating on a defined transition timeline. *Recommended default: yes.*
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:104:**Pivot's approach.** Pivot's BRD articulates role-based access aligned with its divisional sales structure (Enterprise, Venture, Public, Construction Solutions per CRM §3.02 D-3b) and its in-house operations footprint.
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:106:**Recommendation for the merged company.** Adopt the standard Orion 25+ custom role taxonomy with merged-company adaptations: roles support both Pivot's divisional structure and KBM's geographic territories per the two-dimensional model locked in CRM §3.02 D-3a. Operations-specific roles reflect Pivot's in-house operations team plus KBM's outsourced-operations coordination roles (per Operations §3.05).
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:128:**Source:** Cross-references multiple sections — HubSpot (Marketing §3.01 D-1), banking (Financial Management §3.08 D-6), payroll (Financial Management §3.08.8 #9), MillerKnoll integrations (Order Management §3.04 D-7), expense platform (Financial Management §3.08 D-7), KBM REQ-020 Exemplis manufacturer integration (`BRD_SystemSetupConfiguration_v1.0.md` §6)
_Unification/07 - System Setup & Configuration.md:130:**KBM's approach.** KBM's source materials specify integration patterns for ServiceNet, ServiceTime, Coupa (evaluation pending), MillerKnoll Quote Tool, MillerKnoll Exemplis manufacturer integration (KBM REQ-020), Stripe, Paylocity, West Coast Community Bank, Google Drive.
