   479	Pivot currently collects job site requirements through various manual processes depending on project complexity\. Information about elevators, parking availability, access restrictions, and installation conditions is gathered through project team visits and documented in various systems\. This data then feeds into labor quote processes where estimators must consider site\-specific factors in their calculations\.
   480	
   481	The current process lacks standardization for requirements collection and often relies on informal communication between team members\. Job site analysis information may be captured in Workfront projects, email communications, or estimator notes, creating inconsistency in data quality and availability for quote accuracy\.
   482	
   483	3\.02\.03 Orion/NetSuite Solution
   484	
   485	Orion/NetSuite provides integrated requirements management through its requirement engine administration and job site analysis record functionality\. The solution enables standardized collection of job site requirements through configurable forms and mobile\-friendly interfaces that ensure consistent data capture across all projects\.
   486	
   487	The requirements management capabilities integrate directly with labor quote processes, ensuring that site\-specific factors are automatically considered in estimation calculations\. Job site analysis records provide centralized storage for all site\-related information, accessible to estimators, project managers, and installation teams throughout the project lifecycle\.
