_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:701:Pivot requires accommodation through custom AP automation workflow for standalone expense vendor bills\. This custom solution will be scoped for Phase 1 inclusion, pending timeline and budget analysis\. Pending decision based on offered solutions\.
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:703:__Email\-to\-Vendor\-Bill Automation:__
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:708:3. Attach PDF to vendor bill record
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:712:The custom automation will leverage NetSuite's email integration framework to monitor the dedicated inbox and extract vendor, amount, date, and GL account information from PDF attachments\. Automated workflows will create vendor bill records with proper approval routing based on configurable thresholds and GL account classifications\. The solution will include exception handling for invoices that cannot be parsed automatically, routing them to a manual review queue\.
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:715:Auto\-created vendor bills will be placed in unapproved state and routed through configurable approval workflows\. Approvers will receive notifications, can review bills with attached PDFs in NetSuite Orion, and approve/reject directly in the system\. Upon approval, bills post automatically to GL\. This eliminates the manual email\-based approval process and ensures bills are tracked in the system from receipt through payment\.
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:720:__Future Phase: Vendor Invoice Follow\-Up:__
_Unification/working/pivot-brds-md/Financial_Management.md:721:Automated vendor invoice follow\-up capability \(tracking expected invoices, sending reminders to vendors\) is acknowledged as a valuable future enhancement but is planned for Phase 2 or Phase 3 implementation\.
